            <div xml:id="d77">

                <pb facs="0098" n="84" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg84"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.34/261</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Director of the Office of Far Eastern
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Under Secretary of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stettinius</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-05-26">May 26, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>With reference to my memorandum of May 23, I called Captain Daniel, USN, on the
                    telephone today, and with regard to our previous conversation on the subject of
                    the request of the Chinese Government for the transfer, under Lend-Lease, of
                    four destroyers and four mine layers, I said that I assumed that no hasty action
                    in the matter would be taken. Captain Daniel confirmed this supposition and said
                    that no commitments had been made. I said that Mr. Hull was interested in the
                    subject and that I expected to confer with him within the next few days and that
                    I would then inform Captain Daniel, for the information of Admiral King, of Mr.
                    Hull’s position. Captain Daniel replied, “Aye, Aye, Sir”.</p>
                <p>I shall be prepared to discuss this subject with the Secretary whenever you and
                    he find it convenient.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph</hi> C. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
